1
00:00:10,093 --> 00:00:11,679
YOU LOOK CUTE IN BUBBLES.

2
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:14,389
AH, YOU'RE JUST ALL LIQUORED UP.

3
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:17,351
( knock on door )

4
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:18,727
Joey:
HEY, IT'S ME.

5
00:00:18,769 --> 00:00:20,061
I'M COMING IN.

6
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:29,613
I'VE HAD A VERY LONG, HARD DAY.

7
00:00:29,655 --> 00:00:31,114
I'M GETTING CHICKEN.
YOU WANT SOME?

8
00:00:31,156 --> 00:00:32,366
NO, THANKS. NO CHICKEN.

9
00:00:32,407 --> 00:00:33,367
BYE-BYE THEN.

10
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:35,035
OKAY.

11
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:36,662
YOU SURE? SOME EXTRA CRISPY?

12
00:00:36,704 --> 00:00:37,788
DIRTY RICE? BEANS?

13
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:38,998
FOR THE LAST TIME, NO.

14
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:40,332
GET OUT. GET OUT, JOEY.

15
00:00:40,374 --> 00:00:42,292
ALL RIGHT.

16
00:00:44,336 --> 00:00:45,963
( gasping )

17
00:00:46,005 --> 00:00:46,964
ARE YOU OKAY?

18
00:00:47,006 --> 00:00:48,757
I'M SO SORRY. HE WOULDN'T LEAVE.

19
00:00:48,799 --> 00:00:49,758
HE KEPT ASKING

20
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:50,968
IF I WANTED CHICKEN.

21
00:00:51,010 --> 00:00:52,803
CHICKEN?

22
00:00:52,845 --> 00:00:55,723
I COULD EAT SOME CHICKEN.

23
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:57,265
HEY, JOE!

24
00:01:00,561 --> 00:01:03,146
YEAH, COULD I GET A THREE-PIECE,
SOME COLE SLAW

25
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:04,565
AND SOME BEANS AND A COKE...

26
00:01:04,606 --> 00:01:05,607
( screaming )

27
00:01:05,649 --> 00:01:07,860
...DIET COKE.

28
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:21,540
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

29
00:01:21,582 --> 00:01:23,834
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

30
00:01:23,876 --> 00:01:26,879
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

31
00:01:26,921 --> 00:01:31,466
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

32
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:34,553
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

33
00:01:34,595 --> 00:01:37,056
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

34
00:01:37,096 --> 00:01:40,935
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

35
00:01:40,976 --> 00:01:45,064
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

36
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:50,069
HEY!

37
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,194
HEY!
HEY, PHEEBS!

38
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:52,738
OH, I HAVE TO TELL
YOU THIS STORY.

39
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:55,783
I WAS COMING OVER HERE
AND THIS CAB DRIVER...

40
00:01:55,824 --> 00:01:57,034
WAS HIS NAME ANGUS?

41
00:01:57,076 --> 00:01:58,493
( all laughing )

42
00:01:58,535 --> 00:01:59,787
WHAT?

43
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:02,205
HE WAS THIS CAB DRIVER
WE HAD IN LONDON.

44
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:03,248
OH. HA-HA-HA.

45
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:04,833
ALL RIGHT, ANYWAY...

46
00:02:04,875 --> 00:02:06,961
Monica:
WHAT WAS THAT PLACE

47
00:02:07,002 --> 00:02:08,336
THAT PUB HE TOOK US TO?

48
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:09,504
THE WHEAT SHEAF.

49
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:11,298
AND THEY HAD THAT BEER,
THAT, UH...

50
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:12,340
BODDINGTON'S.

51
00:02:12,382 --> 00:02:13,842
BODDINGTON'S.
BODDINGTON'S.

52
00:02:13,884 --> 00:02:15,052
THAT'S IT, BABY.

53
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:18,847
OH, PHEEBS WAS GOING
TO TELL A STORY.

54
00:02:18,889 --> 00:02:21,767
OKAY, SO, HE HAD
A REALLY FUNNY HAT.

55
00:02:21,809 --> 00:02:24,352
I DON'T WANT TO TALK ABOUT IT.

56
00:02:25,646 --> 00:02:26,855
HEY.

57
00:02:26,897 --> 00:02:27,898
HEY, ROSS.

58
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:29,190
BODDINGTON'S.

59
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:30,150
YEAH!
YEAH!

60
00:02:30,191 --> 00:02:31,234
OH, MAN.

61
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:33,988
THAT WAS GOOD BEER.

62
00:02:34,029 --> 00:02:35,405
YOU KNOW, I'D WALK
BACK TO LONDON

63
00:02:35,447 --> 00:02:37,240
FOR ANOTHER FROSTY ONE
OF THOSE BAD BOYS.

64
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:38,867
YOU KNOW, I THINK
THEY HAVE THOSE

65
00:02:38,909 --> 00:02:40,869
AT THAT BRITISH PUB
BY THE TRADE CENTER.

66
00:02:40,911 --> 00:02:42,997
LATER.

67
00:02:43,038 --> 00:02:44,957
ISN'T RACHEL SUPPOSED
TO BE BACK BY NOW?

68
00:02:44,999 --> 00:02:46,500
HER PLANE GOT
DELAYED IN ATHENS

69
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:48,543
BUT, ACTUALLY, SHE SHOULD
BE HERE BY NOW.

70
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:49,837
S-SO YOU TALKED TO HER?

71
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:51,546
DID SHE... DID SHE SOUND MAD?

72
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:53,757
NO, BUT SHE LIKES ME.

73
00:02:54,925 --> 00:02:56,384
YOU ABANDONED HER ON A PLANE.

74
00:02:56,426 --> 00:02:59,387
OKAY, I DID NOT ABANDON RACHEL,
OKAY?

75
00:02:59,429 --> 00:03:02,057
EMILY SHOWED UP AT THE AIRPORT.

76
00:03:02,099 --> 00:03:03,517
I HAD TO GO AFTER HER.

77
00:03:03,558 --> 00:03:05,519
I MEAN, I DID WHAT I HAD TO DO.

78
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:06,520
SHE'S MY WIFE.

79
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:08,229
RACHEL IS MY WIFE, YOU KNOW.

80
00:03:08,271 --> 00:03:10,774
EMILY!

81
00:03:10,816 --> 00:03:13,861
EMILY IS MY WIFE.

82
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:17,156
MAN, WHAT IS THAT?

83
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:19,574
SO YOU STILL HAVEN'T HEARD
FROM EMILY?

84
00:03:19,616 --> 00:03:21,785
NO, NOT SINCE I LOST HER
AT THE AIRPORT.

85
00:03:21,827 --> 00:03:24,079
I CAN'T BELIEVE
SHE CAN OUTRUN YOU, MAN.

86
00:03:24,121 --> 00:03:27,206
HEY, SHE'S FAST, OKAY?

87
00:03:27,248 --> 00:03:29,543
OH, YOU THINK
YOU CAN BEAT ME?

88
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:31,045
LET'S GO, OUTSIDE!

89
00:03:33,047 --> 00:03:34,840
HI.

90
00:03:34,882 --> 00:03:36,257
RACHEL!
HI!

91
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:40,054
RACH, RACH, I AM SO SORRY.

92
00:03:40,095 --> 00:03:42,014
I AM SO, SO SORRY.

93
00:03:42,056 --> 00:03:43,098
OH, ROSS, COME ON.

94
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:44,808
YOU JUST DID
WHAT YOU HAD TO DO.

95
00:03:46,476 --> 00:03:47,728
THAT'S IT?

96
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:49,063
YOU'RE NOT MAD?

97
00:03:49,104 --> 00:03:50,689
I MEAN,
IT MUST HAVE BEEN TERRIBLE.

98
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:52,983
TERRIBLE? HELL,
I WAS IN GREECE.

99
00:03:53,025 --> 00:03:55,443
THAT WAS A NICE HOTEL.

100
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:56,737
NICE BEACH.

101
00:03:56,778 --> 00:03:58,780
MET THE NICE PEOPLE.

102
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:00,365
NOT TOO SHABBY FOR RACHEL.

103
00:04:03,326 --> 00:04:05,244
SO, WHAT? THAT'S IT?

104
00:04:05,286 --> 00:04:06,538
WELL, YEAH.

105
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:08,373
WE'RE COOL.
TOTALLY COOL.

106
00:04:10,209 --> 00:04:11,250
THANKS, RACH.

107
00:04:11,292 --> 00:04:12,586
OH, YOU'RE THE BEST.

108
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:15,463
OH, NO, YOU'RE THE BEST.

109
00:04:15,505 --> 00:04:19,218
OH, I GOT TO GO
TO THE FLOWER STORE.

110
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:20,468
CHECK IT OUT.

111
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:22,637
NO ONE WILL TELL ME
WHERE EMILY IS.

112
00:04:22,679 --> 00:04:25,473
SO I'M GOING TO SEND
72 LONG-STEMMED RED ROSES

113
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:26,850
TO HER PARENTS' HOUSE.

114
00:04:26,892 --> 00:04:29,269
ONE FOR EACH DAY
THAT I'VE KNOWN AND LOVED HER.

115
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,479
THAT OUGHT TO GET HER
TALKING TO ME AGAIN.

116
00:04:31,521 --> 00:04:34,191
OH, ROSS, WHEN YOU MAKE OUT
THE CARD

117
00:04:34,233 --> 00:04:36,693
BE SURE TO MAKE IT OUT
TO EMILY.

118
00:04:39,571 --> 00:04:40,948
RACH, THAT'S GREAT.

119
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:43,450
IT'S SO GOOD YOU HAD SUCH
A GOOD TIME IN GREECE.

120
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:47,204
WHAT?

121
00:04:47,246 --> 00:04:49,748
I DIDN'T HAVE A GOOD TIME
IN GREECE.

122
00:04:50,874 --> 00:04:52,584
ROSS ABANDONED ME, OKAY?

123
00:04:52,626 --> 00:04:54,502
I COULDN'T GET A PLANE OUT

124
00:04:54,544 --> 00:04:57,172
SO I HAD TO STAY
IN THEIR HONEYMOON SUITE

125
00:04:57,214 --> 00:04:59,507
WITH PEOPLE COMING UP TO ME
ALL THE TIME, GOING

126
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:02,469
"OH, MRS. GELLER, WHY YOU CRY?"

127
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:06,014
I MEAN, IT WAS SO HUMILIATING.

128
00:05:06,056 --> 00:05:08,016
I FELT
LIKE SUCH AN IDIOT.

129
00:05:08,058 --> 00:05:09,517
I MEAN, IT'S ALL MY FAULT.

130
00:05:09,559 --> 00:05:10,852
AND YOU KNOW WHY?

131
00:05:10,894 --> 00:05:14,522
BECAUSE I MAKE
VERY BAD DECISIONS.

132
00:05:14,564 --> 00:05:15,941
OH, THAT'S NOT TRUE.

133
00:05:15,983 --> 00:05:17,525
YES, IT IS. IT IS TRUE.

134
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:19,653
I WENT AFTER ROSS
IN STUPID LONDON.

135
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:22,656
LONDON IS STUPID. STUPID.

136
00:05:24,032 --> 00:05:25,366
PHOEBE, YOU WERE RIGHT.

137
00:05:25,408 --> 00:05:27,327
I SHOULD NEVER HAVE GONE
TO LONDON

138
00:05:27,368 --> 00:05:28,411
AND FROM NOW ON

139
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:30,371
YOU MAKE
ALL MY DECISIONS FOR ME.

140
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:32,415
OH, NO, I DID THAT
FOR SOMEONE ONCE.

141
00:05:32,457 --> 00:05:35,043
I'M NOT COMFORTABLE
HAVING THAT KIND OF POWER

142
00:05:35,085 --> 00:05:36,878
AND CONTROL OVER
SOMEONE'S LIFE.

143
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,213
I'LL DO IT.

144
00:05:38,255 --> 00:05:39,714
Rachel:
THAT'S FINE.

145
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:43,593
SO, MONICA, YOU ARE NOW
IN CHARGE OF MY LOVE LIFE.

146
00:05:44,678 --> 00:05:46,263
OKAY, I GOT TO GO TO WORK.

147
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:59,276
AND RACHEL,
GREAT TO HAVE YOU BACK.

148
00:06:03,404 --> 00:06:05,240
PHEEBS!

149
00:06:11,121 --> 00:06:12,497
ALWAYS A PLEASURE.

150
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:23,925
OH, RACHEL, SWEETIE, LOOK.

151
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:25,093
HERE'S A REALLY
CUTE PICTURE

152
00:06:25,135 --> 00:06:26,594
OF YOU AND JOEY
AT THE RECEPTION.

153
00:06:26,636 --> 00:06:28,055
OH, HE'S MARRIED.

154
00:06:28,096 --> 00:06:29,430
ROSS IS MARRIED.

155
00:06:29,472 --> 00:06:31,599
I STILL CAN'T BELIEVE IT.

156
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:34,102
HONEY, SWEETIE, BY THE EDGES.

157
00:06:34,144 --> 00:06:36,479
I MEAN, I'M JUST GOING
TO HAVE TO ACCEPT IT.

158
00:06:36,521 --> 00:06:37,605
OH!

159
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:38,857
IT'S MY FAULT.

160
00:06:38,899 --> 00:06:40,275
SWEETIE... EDGES...

161
00:06:40,317 --> 00:06:41,442
FINGERS...
SMUDGY...

162
00:06:41,484 --> 00:06:43,153
OH, MY GOD! AH!

163
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:49,784
THAT'S OKAY.

164
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:51,745
I KNOW THAT YOU'RE VERY UPSET
RIGHT NOW.

165
00:06:51,786 --> 00:06:53,205
I KNOW THAT WASN'T ABOUT ME.

166
00:06:53,247 --> 00:06:56,291
I BET IT WAS ABOUT HER
A LITTLE.

167
00:06:56,333 --> 00:06:57,918
IF YOU STOPPED THINKING
ABOUT ROSS

168
00:06:57,959 --> 00:07:00,295
YOU WOULD NOTICE
THERE WERE GREAT GUYS
EVERYWHERE.

169
00:07:00,337 --> 00:07:01,713
NOW, LOOK...

170
00:07:01,755 --> 00:07:02,714
GUNTHER.

171
00:07:02,756 --> 00:07:05,384
I MEAN...

172
00:07:05,424 --> 00:07:07,261
HE'S NICE. HE'S CUTE.

173
00:07:07,302 --> 00:07:09,804
YEAH, I GUESS GUNTHER IS...

174
00:07:09,846 --> 00:07:10,764
OR HOW ABOUT

175
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:12,015
THAT GUY
OVER THERE?

176
00:07:13,558 --> 00:07:14,935
THAT IS THE GUY
YOU FLIRTED WITH

177
00:07:14,976 --> 00:07:16,061
AT THE COUNTER
THAT TIME.

178
00:07:17,187 --> 00:07:19,356
OH, I DON'T KNOW,
I DON'T KNOW.

179
00:07:19,398 --> 00:07:20,607
YOU'RE GOING TO TALK TO HIM.

180
00:07:20,648 --> 00:07:21,608
WE MADE A DEAL.

181
00:07:21,649 --> 00:07:22,817
I MAKE YOUR DECISIONS

182
00:07:22,859 --> 00:07:24,485
AND I SAY YOU'RE GOING
TO TALK TO HIM.

183
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:26,196
ALL RIGHT.

184
00:07:26,238 --> 00:07:27,406
YOU'RE THE BOSS.

185
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:29,991
I GUESS I GOT TO DO
WHAT YOU TELL ME.

186
00:07:30,033 --> 00:07:32,744
SAY THAT TO HIM
AND YOU'RE GOLDEN.

187
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,166
HEY.

188
00:07:38,208 --> 00:07:39,960
HEY, PHEEBS.
HEY, PHEEBS.

189
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:41,420
WE GOT OUR PICTURES
FROM LONDON.

190
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:44,339
HERE'S ALL OF US
AT THE TOWER OF LONDON...

191
00:07:44,381 --> 00:07:46,549
OH, YEAH, THERE WE ALL ARE.

192
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:49,677
YEAH, THERE'S ROSS AND JOEY
AND YOU AND...

193
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:52,013
AND ME.

194
00:07:53,681 --> 00:07:56,143
WE'VE BEEN TALKING
ABOUT LONDON TOO MUCH,
HAVEN'T WE?

195
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:57,311
NO, I'M SORRY.

196
00:07:57,352 --> 00:07:59,146
IT'S JUST
'CAUSE I COULDN'T BE THERE

197
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:01,815
'CAUSE ALL I EVER GET TO DO NOW
IS PREGNANT STUFF.

198
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:03,150
IT JUST BUMS ME OUT.

199
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:04,901
SORRY.
SORRY.

200
00:08:04,943 --> 00:08:06,694
WHAT HAPPENED?

201
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:08,071
WELL, YOU KNOW,
A LITTLE OF THIS

202
00:08:08,113 --> 00:08:09,281
A LITTLE OF THAT.

203
00:08:09,323 --> 00:08:11,825
I GOT MYSELF A DATE
TOMORROW NIGHT.

204
00:08:11,866 --> 00:08:13,201
SEE? DIDN'T I TELL YOU?

205
00:08:13,243 --> 00:08:15,203
YOU'RE GETTING OVER ROSS
ALREADY.

206
00:08:16,663 --> 00:08:18,748
GET OUT.

207
00:08:33,512 --> 00:08:34,889
WHAT TOOK YOU SO LONG?

208
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:36,224
I GOT CAUGHT UP AT WORK

209
00:08:36,266 --> 00:08:37,767
BUT I'M QUITTING TOMORROW.

210
00:08:43,315 --> 00:08:45,150
SO, THANKS FOR
HAVING ME OVER.

211
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:49,196
RACH.

212
00:08:54,368 --> 00:08:55,827
PHEEBS.

213
00:09:03,502 --> 00:09:04,794
SEE YA!

214
00:09:07,964 --> 00:09:09,966
WHAT THE HELL WAS THAT?

215
00:09:10,008 --> 00:09:12,719
PROBABLY SOME
EUROPEAN GOOD-BYE THING

216
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:14,304
HE PICKED UP IN LONDON.

217
00:09:14,346 --> 00:09:15,305
I DON'T...

218
00:09:15,347 --> 00:09:16,639
IT'S NOT EUROPEAN.

219
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:19,100
WELL, IT FELT FRENCH.

220
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:26,525
OH, GOD, I REALLY
HAD A GOOD TIME.

221
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:27,526
YEAH, ME, TOO.

222
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:29,777
( sighing )

223
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:32,322
SO, I GUESS THIS IS IT.

224
00:09:32,364 --> 00:09:33,948
YEAH, UM...

225
00:09:33,990 --> 00:09:36,576
UNLESS YOU WANT
TO COME INSIDE.

226
00:09:36,617 --> 00:09:37,577
YEAH.

227
00:09:37,618 --> 00:09:39,371
OKAY... OH, UH...

228
00:09:39,413 --> 00:09:40,497
YOU KNOW WHAT?

229
00:09:40,539 --> 00:09:42,707
I, UH...
I CAN'T DECIDE THIS.

230
00:09:42,749 --> 00:09:43,875
UM...

231
00:09:45,335 --> 00:09:46,920
OKAY, JUST HOLD
ON A SECOND.

232
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:48,422
YEAH.

233
00:09:51,007 --> 00:09:52,717
UH, HI.

234
00:09:52,759 --> 00:09:54,177
HI.

235
00:09:54,219 --> 00:09:55,178
IS MONICA AROUND?

236
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:56,721
I HAVE TO ASK HER SOMETHING.

237
00:09:56,763 --> 00:09:58,681
DOING HER LAUNDRY.

238
00:09:58,723 --> 00:09:59,974
WHAT'S THAT?

239
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:03,520
IT CAME IN THE
MAIL TODAY.

240
00:10:03,562 --> 00:10:06,231
IT'S 72 LONG-STEMMED RED ROSES

241
00:10:06,273 --> 00:10:10,068
ONE FOR EACH DAY
I'VE KNOWN AND LOVED EMILY

242
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:12,946
CUT UP INTO MULCH.

243
00:10:14,281 --> 00:10:15,656
OH, HONEY,
THAT'S AWFUL.

244
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:18,159
OH, IT'S NOT SO BAD.

245
00:10:18,201 --> 00:10:21,871
MONICA'S GOING
TO MAKE POTPOURRI.

246
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:26,167
I THINK I'M GOING
TO GO WANDER OUT

247
00:10:26,209 --> 00:10:27,877
IN THE RAIN
FOR A WHILE.

248
00:10:27,919 --> 00:10:29,504
BUT IT'S NOT RAINING.

249
00:10:29,546 --> 00:10:33,467
I CAN'T CATCH A BREAK.

250
00:10:33,508 --> 00:10:34,468
YOU KNOW WHAT, ROSS?

251
00:10:34,509 --> 00:10:35,676
YOU'RE NOT GOING
ANYWHERE.

252
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:37,220
YOU'RE GOING TO SIT
RIGHT HERE.

253
00:10:37,262 --> 00:10:38,846
I'M GOING TO MAKE YOU
A CUP OF TEA

254
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:41,015
AND WE'RE GOING TO TALK
THIS WHOLE THING OUT.

255
00:10:41,057 --> 00:10:42,434
ALL RIGHT?

256
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:46,062
HEY, DAVE.

257
00:10:46,104 --> 00:10:47,439
YEAH.

258
00:10:47,481 --> 00:10:49,857
LISTEN, I'M GOING TO
NEED TO TAKE A RAIN CHECK.

259
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:51,610
MY ROOMMATE IS
JUST REALLY SICK.

260
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:52,693
OKAY? BYE.

261
00:10:56,406 --> 00:10:58,617
HONEY, LISTEN...

262
00:10:58,658 --> 00:10:59,742
I KNOW...

263
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:01,786
GOD, I KNOW
THINGS SEEM SO BAD...

264
00:11:01,828 --> 00:11:03,371
RACH?

265
00:11:04,414 --> 00:11:06,416
COULD I TALK TO YOU
JUST FOR A MINUTE?

266
00:11:07,666 --> 00:11:09,752
I DROPPED SOME SOCKS.

267
00:11:09,794 --> 00:11:11,379
YEAH.

268
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:20,054
WHAT IS THE MATTER
WITH YOU?

269
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:21,722
DO YOU WANT TO FALL
INTO THE TRAP?

270
00:11:21,764 --> 00:11:23,808
DO YOU WANT
TO FALL INTO THE TRAP?

271
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:26,978
YOU DID NOT
DROP ANY SOCKS!

272
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:29,230
DAVE TOLD ME
YOU BLEW HIM OFF.

273
00:11:29,272 --> 00:11:30,565
YOU LISTEN TO ME.

274
00:11:30,607 --> 00:11:31,858
I'M CALLING THE SHOTS.

275
00:11:31,899 --> 00:11:34,110
I SAY YOU LEAVE ROSS ALONE
AND GO GET DAVE.

276
00:11:34,152 --> 00:11:36,029
WHAT THE HELL ARE YOU
TRYING TO DO?

277
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:38,697
WELL, ULTIMATELY,
I WAS TRYING...

278
00:11:38,739 --> 00:11:40,408
YOU KNOW, I WANTED...

279
00:11:40,450 --> 00:11:43,662
TO TELL HIM I WAS
STILL IN LOVE WITH HIM.

280
00:11:43,702 --> 00:11:44,787
WHAT?

281
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:46,956
YOU CANNOT TELL HIM THAT.

282
00:11:46,998 --> 00:11:48,625
WHY? WHY NOT?

283
00:11:48,667 --> 00:11:51,461
PEOPLE LOVE
TO HEAR THAT.

284
00:11:51,503 --> 00:11:54,631
I MAKE THE DECISIONS
AND I SAY "NO."

285
00:11:54,673 --> 00:11:55,714
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT?

286
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:57,342
NO, YOU DON'T MAKE
MY DECISIONS

287
00:11:57,384 --> 00:11:59,135
BECAUSE... YOU'RE FIRED.

288
00:11:59,177 --> 00:12:00,136
( gasps )

289
00:12:00,178 --> 00:12:02,013
YOU CAN'T FIRE ME.

290
00:12:02,055 --> 00:12:07,268
I MAKE YOUR DECISIONS AND I SAY
I'M NOT FIRED. HA!

291
00:12:08,645 --> 00:12:09,812
WELL...

292
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:16,403
( gasps )

293
00:12:19,489 --> 00:12:20,532
RACHEL!

294
00:12:20,574 --> 00:12:21,991
COME ON,
LET ME IN.

295
00:12:22,033 --> 00:12:24,452
HAVING SOME TROUBLE?

296
00:12:24,494 --> 00:12:26,371
RACHEL LOCKED THE DOOR.

297
00:12:26,413 --> 00:12:29,583
I'LL KICK THAT DOOR IN
IF YOU GIVE ME A LITTLE SUGAR.

298
00:12:34,087 --> 00:12:35,754
OH! RACHEL!
RA... LET ME IN!

299
00:12:35,796 --> 00:12:36,881
RACHEL?

300
00:12:36,923 --> 00:12:38,466
( pounding )

301
00:12:44,763 --> 00:12:46,099
THANK YOU.

302
00:12:48,435 --> 00:12:51,563
RACHEL... CAN I TALK
TO YOU OUTSIDE FOR A SEC?

303
00:12:51,605 --> 00:12:52,813
NO.

304
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:56,067
I REALLY NEED
TO TALK TO YOU.

305
00:12:56,109 --> 00:12:57,776
WELL, THEN, TALK.

306
00:12:57,818 --> 00:12:59,696
OKAY, I WILL.

307
00:13:02,198 --> 00:13:04,492
REMEMBER THAT THING
THAT WE JUST DISCUSSED

308
00:13:04,534 --> 00:13:05,784
THAT YOU WANTED TO DO?

309
00:13:05,826 --> 00:13:07,245
YES.

310
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:08,663
WHAT THING?

311
00:13:08,705 --> 00:13:10,415
Monica:
WELL...

312
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:14,877
RACHEL WANTS TO TAKE
SWING DANCE LESSONS...

313
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:17,213
WHICH I THINK IS
A REALLY STUPID IDEA.

314
00:13:17,255 --> 00:13:18,423
IT'S DANGEROUS.

315
00:13:18,465 --> 00:13:20,759
SHE'S NEVER GOING TO GET
WHAT SHE WANTS

316
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:22,469
AND WHO KNOWS
WHO SHE MIGHT

317
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:24,679
END UP HURTING?

318
00:13:30,685 --> 00:13:34,773
MONICA'S RIGHT,
SWING DANCING CAN BE TRICKY.

319
00:13:36,274 --> 00:13:37,858
I'M GOING
TO USE THE PHONE.

320
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:39,277
I GOT TO CANCEL

321
00:13:39,319 --> 00:13:42,029
THOSE FIVE GIANT TEDDY BEARS
I SENT TO EMILY.

322
00:13:42,071 --> 00:13:43,906
MY GOD,
THINK OF THE MASSACRE.

323
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:46,493
I'M GOING TO DO IT.

324
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:47,577
ALL RIGHT... RACHEL...

325
00:13:47,619 --> 00:13:48,995
OKAY, I KNOW
YOU THINK I'M CRAZY

326
00:13:49,036 --> 00:13:50,622
BUT BEFORE YOU TELL HIM
YOU LOVE HIM

327
00:13:50,664 --> 00:13:53,082
JUST TRY TO FIND ONE PERSON
WHO THINKS THIS IS A GOOD IDEA

328
00:13:53,124 --> 00:13:54,125
'CAUSE I BET YOU CAN'T.

329
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:55,126
BUT I R...

330
00:13:55,168 --> 00:13:56,210
PLEASE!

331
00:13:57,836 --> 00:13:59,088
ALL RIGHT, FINE.

332
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:01,508
( thud )

333
00:14:03,384 --> 00:14:06,095
JOEY, I'M IN!

334
00:14:06,137 --> 00:14:08,598
( Joey, painfully ):
ALL RIGHT, GOOD DEAL.

335
00:14:13,561 --> 00:14:15,021
HEY...

336
00:14:15,062 --> 00:14:16,022
PHEEBS!
PHOEBE!

337
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:17,398
Rachel:
HEY, PHEEBS.

338
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,650
UH...

339
00:14:18,692 --> 00:14:20,360
OKAY... PHEEBS?

340
00:14:20,401 --> 00:14:22,153
YEAH?
UM...

341
00:14:22,195 --> 00:14:24,030
YOU KNOW HOW THE OTHER DAY
YOU WERE TALKING

342
00:14:24,071 --> 00:14:25,740
ABOUT HOW YOU DIDN'T GET
TO GO TO LONDON

343
00:14:25,782 --> 00:14:27,116
AND YOU WERE FEELING LEFT OUT?

344
00:14:27,158 --> 00:14:28,117
YEAH.

345
00:14:28,159 --> 00:14:29,243
ALL RIGHT, WELL

346
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:31,037
WE ALL FELT REALLY BAD
ABOUT THAT

347
00:14:31,078 --> 00:14:32,455
SO... WE DECIDED

348
00:14:32,497 --> 00:14:34,666
THAT WE SHOULD ALL TAKE
A LITTLE TRIP TOGETHER.

349
00:14:34,708 --> 00:14:37,084
OH, THAT'S SO NICE!

350
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:38,085
HOW GREAT! WHERE?

351
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:39,086
WHERE'S THE TRIP?

352
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:40,338
WELL...

353
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:42,841
WE THOUGHT WE WOULD ALL GO
TO A PICNIC...

354
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:43,591
( gasps )

355
00:14:43,633 --> 00:14:45,218
IN CENTRAL PARK!

356
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:47,512
CENTRAL PARK?

357
00:14:47,554 --> 00:14:49,305
YEAH, ALL OF US, ALL DAY.

358
00:14:49,347 --> 00:14:50,931
THAT SUCKS.

359
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:53,100
THAT'S NOT A TRIP.

360
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:54,602
I JUST CAME
FROM THE PARK.

361
00:14:54,644 --> 00:14:56,437
WHAT ARE WE GOING
TO HIGH-FIVE ABOUT

362
00:14:56,479 --> 00:14:57,980
AT THE STUPID CENTRAL PARK?

363
00:14:58,022 --> 00:14:59,482
WELL, IT'S RIGHT BY MY HOUSE.

364
00:14:59,524 --> 00:15:00,525
ALL RIGHT!

365
00:15:02,068 --> 00:15:03,653
WELL, I'M GOING TO GO HOME

366
00:15:03,695 --> 00:15:06,656
AND BASK IN THE TRIUMPH
OF MY CENTRAL PARK IDEA.

367
00:15:06,698 --> 00:15:07,699
HEY, WHOA!

368
00:15:07,741 --> 00:15:09,992
HOLD ON A SEC THERE, MR. KISSY.

369
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:11,952
YOU KNOW

370
00:15:11,994 --> 00:15:13,788
I'VE BEEN MEANING TO TALK TO YOU

371
00:15:13,830 --> 00:15:16,290
ABOUT THIS WHOLE, LITTLE,
NEW EUROPEAN THING

372
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:17,916
YOU'VE GOT GOING ON

373
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:20,961
AND I JUST NEED TO TELL YOU
IT MAKES ME VERY UNCOMFORTABLE

374
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:23,005
AND I JUST...
YOU KNOW, JUST STOP IT.

375
00:15:23,047 --> 00:15:24,424
WELL, I WAS JUST TRYING

376
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:26,718
TO BRING A LITTLE CULTURE
TO THE GROUP.

377
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:30,221
THAT'S FINE, JUST DON'T
BRING IT IN MY MOUTH.

378
00:15:30,263 --> 00:15:32,014
IT MAKES ME WANT
TO PUKE.

379
00:15:39,105 --> 00:15:41,315
HEY, EVERYBODY,
PHEEBS IS HERE.

380
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:42,316
PHOEBE!
HEY, PHOEBE!

381
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:43,317
HEY, PHEEBS!

382
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:44,944
HEY, PHOEBE,
WHOO!

383
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:47,363
OKAY, WHOO, HI.

384
00:15:47,405 --> 00:15:48,948
OKAY, PHEEBS...
WE DECIDED

385
00:15:48,989 --> 00:15:51,158
THAT THE PICNIC
IDEA WAS A LITTLE...

386
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:53,119
YOU KNOW, IT
DIDN'T HAVE ANY...

387
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:54,287
WELL, IT BLEW.

388
00:15:54,328 --> 00:15:55,954
SO...

389
00:15:55,996 --> 00:15:58,207
WE THOUGHT THAT
THIS AFTERNOON

390
00:15:58,249 --> 00:16:01,419
WE WOULD ALL GO AWAY
FOR THE WHOLE WEEKEND

391
00:16:01,461 --> 00:16:02,754
TO ATLANTIC CITY.

392
00:16:02,796 --> 00:16:04,130
OOH, ATLANTIC CITY!

393
00:16:04,171 --> 00:16:05,924
OH, THAT'S A GREAT PLAN.

394
00:16:05,964 --> 00:16:07,425
WHOSE PLAN WAS THAT?

395
00:16:07,467 --> 00:16:08,635
MINE.

396
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:09,636
( excited gasp )

397
00:16:09,677 --> 00:16:10,637
WAIT.

398
00:16:10,678 --> 00:16:11,638
IT WAS MY PLAN.

399
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:12,806
Joey:
NO...

400
00:16:12,847 --> 00:16:15,266
I SAID WE NEEDED
A NEW PLAN.

401
00:16:15,308 --> 00:16:17,560
AND I CAME UP
WITH ATLANTIC CITY.

402
00:16:17,602 --> 00:16:19,019
WHICH IS THE NEW PLAN.

403
00:16:19,061 --> 00:16:20,521
( disbelieving grunt )

404
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:23,858
OKAY, WELL, WHY
DON'T WE, UM

405
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:25,234
ALL MEET UPSTAIRS
IN AN HOUR?

406
00:16:25,276 --> 00:16:26,569
( excited gasp )

407
00:16:26,611 --> 00:16:28,780
OKAY. OOH, ALL RIGHT,
I'M GOING TO GO PACK.

408
00:16:28,822 --> 00:16:30,573
I'M GOING
TO GO PACK MY ASS OFF.

409
00:16:30,615 --> 00:16:32,116
WHOO!

410
00:16:32,158 --> 00:16:33,827
ALL RIGHT, COME ON,
RACH, LET'S GO.

411
00:16:33,868 --> 00:16:35,161
YEAH, YOU KNOW WHAT?

412
00:16:35,202 --> 00:16:37,121
I'M GOING TO MEET YOU
UPSTAIRS IN A MINUTE.

413
00:16:37,163 --> 00:16:38,164
NO.

414
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:39,916
RACHEL, YOU DIDN'T
FIND ANYONE

415
00:16:39,958 --> 00:16:41,292
SO YOU CAN'T TELL HIM.

416
00:16:41,334 --> 00:16:42,460
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT?

417
00:16:42,502 --> 00:16:43,628
THAT DOESN'T MATTER.

418
00:16:43,670 --> 00:16:45,421
OKAY, RACHEL, DO
YOU HAVE ANY IDEA

419
00:16:45,463 --> 00:16:48,132
HOW PAINFUL IT IS
TO TELL SOMEONE
THAT YOU LOVE THEM

420
00:16:48,174 --> 00:16:49,801
AND NOT HAVE THEM
SAY IT BACK?

421
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:54,430
I-I DON'T CARE.

422
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,517
OKAY.

423
00:16:57,558 --> 00:16:58,935
I-I CAN'T WATCH.

424
00:17:14,074 --> 00:17:16,034
WHATCHA READING?

425
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:18,579
PAPER.

426
00:17:18,621 --> 00:17:20,080
YEAH? WHAT'S
IT ABOUT?

427
00:17:21,415 --> 00:17:25,712
EVENTS... FROM AROUND THE GLOBE.

428
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:26,713
OKAY.

429
00:17:26,754 --> 00:17:28,715
( chuckles )

430
00:17:28,756 --> 00:17:31,050
UH... ROSS,
YOU KNOW WHAT?

431
00:17:31,091 --> 00:17:31,968
THERE'S SOMETHING
THAT I...

432
00:17:32,010 --> 00:17:33,344
THAT I HAVE TO
TALK TO YOU ABOUT

433
00:17:33,386 --> 00:17:34,888
AND EVERYBODY'S BEEN SAYING
THAT I SHOULDN'T TELL YOU

434
00:17:34,929 --> 00:17:36,055
BUT I-I THINK THEY'RE WRONG.

435
00:17:36,096 --> 00:17:37,682
I MEAN, YOU KNOW HOW
PEOPLE CAN BE WRONG.

436
00:17:37,724 --> 00:17:38,766
SURE.

437
00:17:38,808 --> 00:17:40,142
ONCE, AT WORK, I...
( laughs )

438
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:42,687
I THOUGHT CARBON DATING
OF FOSSILIZED...

439
00:17:42,729 --> 00:17:43,813
OKAY, ROSS, I'M
REALLY TRYING

440
00:17:43,855 --> 00:17:45,439
TO TELL YOU
SOMETHING HERE.

441
00:17:45,481 --> 00:17:46,440
OH, UH...

442
00:17:46,482 --> 00:17:47,441
YEAH.

443
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:48,442
OKAY.

444
00:17:48,484 --> 00:17:50,069
GO AHEAD.

445
00:17:50,110 --> 00:17:51,571
UM... OKAY.

446
00:17:51,612 --> 00:17:54,323
I THINK I'M-I'M JUST GO...
I'M JUST GOING TO SAY IT.

447
00:17:54,365 --> 00:17:55,742
I'M JUST GOING
TO SAY IT.

448
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:57,035
UH...

449
00:17:58,369 --> 00:17:59,704
( sighs )

450
00:18:03,875 --> 00:18:07,211
I'M STILL IN LOVE
WITH YOU... ROSS.

451
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:18,180
WOW.

452
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:19,223
UH...

453
00:18:20,725 --> 00:18:22,142
HUH, I'M-I'M...

454
00:18:22,184 --> 00:18:25,021
WOW, I'M NOT SURE
WHAT TO DO WITH THAT RIGHT NOW.

455
00:18:25,063 --> 00:18:26,397
( laughing )

456
00:18:31,444 --> 00:18:32,987
WH-WHAT? WAS THAT A JOKE?

457
00:18:33,029 --> 00:18:34,113
'CAUSE IT'S MEAN.

458
00:18:35,448 --> 00:18:36,866
( laughing )

459
00:18:36,908 --> 00:18:38,743
I'M SO DEAD SERIOUS.

460
00:18:39,911 --> 00:18:41,537
I'M TOTALLY SERIOUS.

461
00:18:41,579 --> 00:18:43,497
WHY ARE YOU LAUGHING?
BECAU...

462
00:18:43,539 --> 00:18:45,499
( laughing )

463
00:18:45,541 --> 00:18:47,710
BECAUSE I
JUST HEARD IT.

464
00:18:47,752 --> 00:18:49,629
I HEARD IT AND
IT'S RIDICULOUS!

465
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:51,171
I MEAN...
YOU'RE MARRIED.

466
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:53,549
YOU'RE MARRIED AND
IT'S JUST RIDICULOUS

467
00:18:53,591 --> 00:18:56,302
AND IT'S, LIKE... IT'S,
LIKE, WHEN I SAID IT

468
00:18:56,343 --> 00:18:59,931
I JUST SORT OF, LIKE,
I FLOATED UP OUT
OF MY BODY, YOU KNOW

469
00:18:59,973 --> 00:19:02,892
AN-AND, THEN... AND, THEN, I
HEARD MYSELF SAY IT

470
00:19:02,934 --> 00:19:05,019
AND, THEN, THE
FLOATING RACHEL...

471
00:19:06,896 --> 00:19:09,857
WAS, LIKE, "YOU ARE
SUCH AN IDIOT!"

472
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:15,404
WELL... WELL, I AM MARRIED...

473
00:19:15,446 --> 00:19:17,031
I KNOW.

474
00:19:17,073 --> 00:19:20,827
EVEN THOUGH I HAVEN'T SPOKEN
TO MY WIFE SINCE THE WEDDING.

475
00:19:20,868 --> 00:19:22,369
( laughing )

476
00:19:24,038 --> 00:19:27,333
I'M SORRY,
THAT'S NOT FUNNY.

477
00:19:27,374 --> 00:19:30,628
ACTUALLY, IT-IT KIND OF IS.

478
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:32,212
( chuckling )

479
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:35,842
MY WIFE WON'T RETURN MY CALLS.

480
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:37,217
( laughing )

481
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:40,178
I DON'T KNOW
WHERE MY WIFE IS.

482
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:41,347
OH, DARN.

483
00:19:41,388 --> 00:19:42,723
( laughing )

484
00:19:44,433 --> 00:19:46,393
"HEY, ROSS,
WHERE'S THE MISSUS?"

485
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:47,937
"DON'T KNOW."

486
00:19:47,979 --> 00:19:49,480
( laughing )

487
00:19:49,522 --> 00:19:51,482
OH... GOD.

488
00:19:51,524 --> 00:19:52,859
OH...

489
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,152
OKAY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

490
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:56,236
DO YOU THINK... UH,
DO YOU THINK YOU COULD

491
00:19:56,278 --> 00:19:58,531
JUST KIND OF FORGET
THAT I TOLD YOU THIS?

492
00:20:00,407 --> 00:20:04,411
WELL, I KIND OF HAVE TO,
I MEAN, 'CAUSE THE THING IS...

493
00:20:04,453 --> 00:20:05,788
WELL, THE THING IS...

494
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:08,332
THAT... YOU KNOW, THAT
YOU'RE MARRIED TO EMILY.

495
00:20:10,751 --> 00:20:13,046
THAT IS WHAT THE THING IS.

496
00:20:17,299 --> 00:20:19,259
OH, GOD.

497
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:20,720
THING... ROSS...

498
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:23,139
THINGS AREN'T GOING TO BE
WEIRD BETWEEN US, RIGHT?

499
00:20:23,181 --> 00:20:25,058
I MEAN, WAS THAT JUST
THE STUPIDEST THING,
ME TELLING YOU THAT?

500
00:20:25,099 --> 00:20:26,059
NO, NO, NO.

501
00:20:26,100 --> 00:20:28,519
GOD, I MEAN, I'M GLAD YOU DID.

502
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:32,565
LOOK, IF-IF NOTHING ELSE,
IT'S-IT'S ALWAYS GREAT

503
00:20:32,606 --> 00:20:34,901
WHEN SOMEONE TELLS YOU
THEY LOVE YOU.

504
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:37,319
R... THAT'S WHAT I SAID!

505
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:41,824
ROSS, THANK YOU
FOR BEING SO NICE.

506
00:20:41,866 --> 00:20:43,367
NO, THANK YOU FOR...

507
00:20:45,578 --> 00:20:46,537
THANK YOU.

508
00:20:46,579 --> 00:20:47,580
( happy sigh )

509
00:20:49,082 --> 00:20:50,041
OKAY, LET'S GO!

510
00:20:50,083 --> 00:20:51,667
YEAH, ATLANTIC CITY!

511
00:20:51,709 --> 00:20:53,293
Ross:
COME ON.

512
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:55,462
ATLANTIC CITY, BABY.

513
00:20:55,504 --> 00:20:57,423
OOH, LET'S ROLL
SOME BONES.

514
00:20:57,464 --> 00:20:58,424
HEY, JOEY

515
00:20:58,465 --> 00:21:00,218
HIGH-FIVE FOR ROLLING BONES.

516
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:01,510
( howling )

517
00:21:01,552 --> 00:21:03,470
OW!

518
00:21:03,512 --> 00:21:04,471
OH!

519
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:07,225
UH, PHEEBS,
YOU'RE LEAKING.

520
00:21:07,265 --> 00:21:09,435
OH, MY GOD,
YOUR WATER BROKE.

521
00:21:09,476 --> 00:21:11,562
OH... OKAY.
OH...

522
00:21:11,604 --> 00:21:13,272
ALL RIGHT,
WELL, DON'T WORRY.

523
00:21:13,313 --> 00:21:14,314
I CALL SHOTGUN.

524
00:21:14,356 --> 00:21:16,192
PHEEBS!

525
00:21:16,234 --> 00:21:18,694
WE HAVE TO TAKE YOU
TO THE HOSPITAL NOW.

526
00:21:18,736 --> 00:21:19,946
Ross:
PHEEBS

527
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:22,531
PHEEBS, THE BABIES
ARE COMING NOW.

528
00:21:22,573 --> 00:21:25,325
HONEY, HIGH-FIVE,
THE BABIES ARE COMING.

529
00:21:25,367 --> 00:21:27,203
( whooping )
HEY, WAIT...

530
00:21:27,245 --> 00:21:29,247
REMEMBER WHEN MY WATER BROKE?

531
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:30,790
( whooping )

532
00:21:34,835 --> 00:21:36,462
PHOEBE'S GOING TO
HAVE HER BABIES.

533
00:21:36,503 --> 00:21:38,965
I KNOW, IT'S...
BEAUTIFUL AND AMAZING.

534
00:21:45,930 --> 00:21:47,723
YOU KNOW WHAT ELSE
I CAN'T BELIEVE?

535
00:21:47,765 --> 00:21:50,851
I HAD TO KISS PHOEBE AND RACHEL
EVERY TIME I LEFT THE ROOM.

536
00:21:50,893 --> 00:21:53,604
I MEAN, IT'S TOO BAD
THEY DIDN'T SEE US HAVING SEX.

537
00:21:53,646 --> 00:21:56,314
DO YOU KNOW ANYTHING
ABOUT WOMEN?

538
00:21:56,356 --> 00:21:58,609
NO.

539
00:21:58,651 --> 00:21:59,485
IT'S ALL RIGHT.

540
00:21:59,526 --> 00:22:01,403
OKAY.

541
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:04,406
